# 25. Parallel Development Strategy

Parallel work is encouraged whenever module dependencies permit.

Typical parallel streams include:

### Backend

- Authentication
- Business
- Membership

### Database

- Migrations
- RLS
- Functions

### Mobile

- Customer App
- Employee App

### Web

- Business Portal

### QA

- Test automation
- UAT preparation

### DevOps

- CI/CD
- Infrastructure
- Monitoring

Cross-module ownership rules remain in effect.

---

# 26. Phase Gates

Each implementation phase must satisfy:

- Definition of Done;
- mandatory tests;
- required reviews;
- documentation updates;
- UAT readiness;
- rollback validation.

A phase may not begin until all mandatory gates from the previous phase have been completed unless an explicit exception is approved by the Solution Architect.

---

# 27. Release Alignment

Every implementation phase should produce a potentially releasable increment.

Major production releases should align with:

- completed business capabilities;
- completed UAT;
- Release Strategy;
- Production Readiness.

Incomplete business workflows should remain protected by feature flags.

---

# 28. Risk Management

Implementation risks should be reviewed continuously.

Typical risks include:

- architectural drift;
- dependency expansion;
- ownership violations;
- documentation drift;
- insufficient testing;
- scope creep.

Each identified risk should have:

- owner;
- mitigation plan;
- review date;
- current status.

---

# 29. Success Criteria

Implementation is considered successful when:

- Blueprint remains authoritative;
- Engineering standards are followed;
- module ownership is preserved;
- UAT passes;
- production readiness is achieved;
- documentation remains synchronized with implementation.

---

# 30. Definition of Implementation Order Ready

The Implementation Order is considered ready when:

- implementation phases are defined;
- dependencies are respected;
- parallel work is identified;
- phase gates are defined;
- release alignment is defined;
- risk management is documented;
- success criteria are defined.

This document becomes the authoritative implementation sequencing guide following Blueprint Freeze v1.0.